[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: UniRide Vision - Lab 2 (Mustafa Ur Rahman, SU-24-01-002-088, Section 02)

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Problem statement

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PS-001
STATEMENT: Students, staff and parents depend on about 25 university buses on Peshawar routes every day. Seats are written in a paper register and fees are paid at a counter, so the transport office spends about three days each semester just registering seats. Passengers cannot tell where a bus is or whether it is full, so some buses run overcrowded while others run nearly empty. Fee records are hard to verify, which leads to repeated disputes between students and the accounts office. Parents cannot find out whether their child has boarded. The university has no reliable data on how many people use each route.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Vision statement

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VIS-001
STATEMENT: For students, staff and parents who need dependable and predictable daily transport, UniRide is a campus transport management system that lets users book and cancel seats, check fee status and follow bus status in one place. Unlike paper registers and counter payments, UniRide gives the transport office live seat availability and demand data for every route.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Objectives

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OBJ-001
STATEMENT: Faster seat registration. Measure: staff working time spent registering seats at semester start. Target: from about three working days to under two hours within one term.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OBJ-002
STATEMENT: Fewer fee disputes. Measure: number of fee disputes handled by the accounts office per month. Target: at least 60% fewer within two terms.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: OBJ-003
STATEMENT: Less overcrowding. Measure: share of trips with more passengers than seats. Target: under 3% of trips within two terms.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Scope

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.1 In scope

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-IN-001
STATEMENT: Seat booking and cancellation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-IN-002
STATEMENT: Fee payment status per student.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-IN-003
STATEMENT: Trip start and end reporting by drivers.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-IN-004
STATEMENT: Passenger list per bus for gate security.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.2 Out of scope

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-OUT-001
STATEMENT: Route planning and optimisation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-OUT-002
STATEMENT: Vehicle maintenance management.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-OUT-003
STATEMENT: Driver payroll.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCO-OUT-004
STATEMENT: Building a payment gateway.

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]
